[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105493,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Inclusion body fibromatosis is a benign myofibroblastic tumour with recurrent potential, characterized by intracytoplasmic eosinophilic inclusions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105494,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105495,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105496,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> infantile digital fibroma/fibromatosis; recurring digital fibrous tumour(s) of childhood; recurring digital fibroma(s) of childhood/infancy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105497,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "<p>Classic (digital) inclusion body fibromatosis; non-classic (extradigital) inclusion body fibromatosis</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-20T15:24:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105498,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Classically, these tumours arise from the dorsal/dorsolateral distal to mid portion of the fingers and toes, although they rarely involve the thumb, great toe, hand, or foot; extra-digital locations (extremities, tongue, breast) are rare {18830128; 840560; 3892466}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105499,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The typical presentation is a painless, dome-shaped to polypoid cutaneous lesion that can occur multiply (multinodular or metachronous on ipsilateral digits) {4344937; 840560; 3835952; 18830128}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105500,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours arise equally in boys and girls aged &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;years; most occur during the first year of life and about 30% are congenital, although adult tumours are rare {18830128; 3892466; 840560; 3835952}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105501,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105502,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105503,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are small (&lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm), nodular, firm, and rubbery, with a fibrous, off-white to grey cut surface {840560; 3835952; 18830128}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105504,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are dermal-based lesions composed of spindled myofibroblastic cells arranged in short to medium-length fascicles, sometimes with a whorled or storiform arrangement. The fascicles are often arranged perpendicularly to the epidermis, surrounding skin adnexal structures, with variable collagen content {4344937; 3892466}. The nuclei are cytologically bland and there are typically intracytoplasmic pale-pink to red inclusions that may be paranuclear and can indent the nucleus {14322942; 3892466}. Trichrome and Movat&rsquo;s pentachrome stains can help highlight these inclusions, staining them red and pink, respectively {18830128}. The inclusions are composed of actin-rich myofilaments that stain for SMA, calponin, and sometimes caldesmon {18830128; 3811906; 6253042; 1310240; 24117680}. Multinucleated giant cells can occasionally be seen in superficial dermis {1946077}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105505,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plump spindled to polygonal cells and a collagenous matrix are seen, occasionally with scattered intracytoplasmic inclusions {21986179}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105506,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105507,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a bland, dermal-based, myofibroblastic spindle cell tumour with intracytoplasmic pink-red inclusions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105508,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105509,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 481,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours have a high risk of recurrence (as high as 75%) but are cured with complete surgical excision {215963; 3892466; 18830128; 8583050; 9493986; 17273037; 21276743}. Spontaneous regression has also been described {17542881}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]